+## Post-Implementation Polish (always)
+
+After the final review is clean and its fixes are committed, but BEFORE
+deleting the workspace or finishing the branch, run the
+post-implementation-polish pipeline over the whole branch. Do not skip it
+and do not ask the user.
+
+You are inline because no subagent tool exists, so you run it yourself:
+load post-implementation-polish and execute all six phases in order —
+three review rounds with fixes, the idiomatic pass, /cleanup, then strip
+and humanize comments. Skip a later review round only when the previous
+round came back clean. Commit between phases, and ledger each phase as
+`Polish: <phase> — <result>`. If a phase surfaces a Critical or Important
+finding, fix it under TDD like any other finding and re-run that phase;
+after 10 iterations across the whole stage, stop and surface to your human
+partner.
+
+If a subagent tool is in fact available, you should not be in this skill —
+route to superpowers:subagent-driven-development, which dispatches polish
+using the agent type named on the plan's `Polish:` line.
+
